@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity  // Optional in Spring Boot — security auto-configured anyway
public class SecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain securityFilterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        // Your custom security configuration
        return http.build();
    }
}
```

When you provide a `SecurityFilterChain` bean, Spring Boot's default security auto-configuration backs off, so your configuration takes over.
